_model: definition
---
title: Definition 11
---
order: 11
---
short_label: XI.Def.11
---
statement: A <i>solid angle</i> is the inclination constituted by more than two lines which meet one another and are not in the same surface, towards all the lines, that is, a <i>solid angle</i> is that which is contained by more than two plane angles which are not in the same plane and are constructed to one point.
---
body:

